# A lens constraining its input with a default: input must be _, and what the lens copies is the defaulted disjunction, not a value.
-- source.cue --
b: string
-- target.cue --
a: string
-- lens.cue --
input: {b: *"d" | string}
result: {a: input.b}
-- out --
not total
input is {b: *"d" | string}, a constraint on what the lens receives; a lens's input must be _, so that the source schema alone says what its instances are (rule input-constrained) @ lens.cue:1:1
result.a is *"d" | string, a disjunction rather than a value; a result field must have one concrete value (rule not-a-value) @ lens.cue:2:13
